{
  "rationale": "Iteration 0 has no race data or evaluator feedback, so this is a conservative baseline built from the contract. Geometry: five 8 mm sensors spaced 1 cm apart across the front of the robot (y = 0.04 m, ahead of the axle) cover the 25 mm tape with some redundancy. Using the small footprint gives sharper position resolution than the larger sizes. Symmetric weights of -2, -1, 0, 1, 2 give a signal that is zero when the line is centred and sign-correct (positive = left). Wheel track 0.12 m, wheel radius 0.03 m, body 0.12 x 0.16 m and mass 0.8 kg are mid-range values that keep yaw inertia moderate for responsive turning. Controller: base_speed 1.6 targets about 1.3 to 1.5 m/s, which is needed to finish within 3 s. kp 2.0 gives a proportional steering response without overshoot at this speed (wheel differential is roughly 2 x 350 x kp x signal). ki 0.05 is a small integral term to remove steady bias such as the motor mismatch. kd 0.1 damps oscillation. line_loss 'last_direction' lets the robot recover toward the side it last saw the line. Expected result: completion on the development tracks, with rms_error well under 0.03 m and few or no line-loss events. Hypotheses to test: (1) if max_error approaches the off-track limit on the slalom, kp is too low or base_speed too high; (2) if steering_oscillation is high, kd or kp is too high; (3) if completion_time exceeds about 3 s, base_speed needs raising. Measurements requested: all available metrics.",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": -0.02, "y": 0.04},
      {"x": -0.01, "y": 0.04},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.04},
      {"x": 0.01, "y": 0.04},
      {"x": 0.02, "y": 0.04}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.008,
    "wheel_track": 0.12,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "body_width": 0.12,
    "body_length": 0.16,
    "mass": 0.8
  },
  "controller": {
    "base_speed": 1.6,
    "kp": 2.0,
    "ki": 0.05,
    "kd": 0.1,
    "sensor_weights": [-2.0, -1.0, 0.0, 1.0, 2.0],
    "line_loss": "last_direction"
  },
  "observation_request": {
    "measurements": [
      "completion",
      "progress",
      "completion_time",
      "rms_error",
      "max_error",
      "line_loss_events",
      "steering_oscillation",
      "control_effort",
      "controller_errors",
      "noise_robustness"
    ]
  },
  "_presentation": {
    "entity0": {
      "label": "Baseline 5-sensor robot",
      "notes": "Conservative first candidate: five 8 mm front sensors, symmetric weights, base_speed 1.6, kp 2.0, small ki and kd. No race data yet, so values come from the contract's mid-range and the speed needed to finish in 3 s."
    }
  }
}
